1.  Consider the composition of your scene. Utilize the rule of thirds to create a balanced and visually appealing image. Experiment with different angles and perspectives to find the most interesting vantage point. 2.  Pay attention to depth of field. Blurting elements in the foreground or background can draw the viewer’s eye into the image and create a sense of depth. 3.  Shoot in a landscape orientation to capture more of the scene and create a wider, more immersive view. 4.  Experiment with different lighting conditions.  Golden hour offers beautiful, warm light, but other times of day can also work well, especially during overcast conditions.

